# MogaFace does not require any environment variables yet.
#
# The current facial-analysis pipeline (Phases 1-21) runs entirely in the
# browser: no server-side API keys, database, or third-party service is
# involved. This file exists as a placeholder for future phases —
# see ARCHITECTURE.md ("Future layers") for what each variable below will do
# once implemented. Do not add real secrets to this file; copy it to
# .env.local (already gitignored) and fill in real values there instead.

# --- Trusted analysis-session persistence (lib/analysis-session/) ---
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION (NODE_ENV=production, i.e. a real Vercel deployment).
# Production requires shared, persistent analysis-session storage — the
# in-memory fallback is development-only. If either variable below is
# missing or NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL is not a well-formed https URL while
# NODE_ENV=production, POST /api/analysis-session and
# POST /api/generate-illustration FAIL CLOSED with a generic 503 — they do
# NOT fall back to the in-memory store, and the illustration endpoint never
# calls the image provider in that state (see
# lib/analysis-session/store.ts's AnalysisPersistenceUnavailableError).
#
# Default: unset. In development only (NODE_ENV !== "production"), leaving
# these unset is fine: both endpoints fall back to an in-memory store — NOT
# shared across separate serverless invocations, so still not what a real
# deployment should ever run on (see the module comment in
# lib/analysis-session/store.ts). To configure real persistence: run the
# migration in supabase/migrations/ (see that file's own header for how),
# then set both of these from your Supabase project's API settings, in
# Vercel's environment variables for the production deployment.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=        # Project URL, https://<ref>.supabase.co (a pasted .../rest/v1 suffix is also accepted). Not a secret.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=       # SECRET — the service_role key, not the anon key. Server-only; bypasses Row Level Security; never commit a real key; put it in .env.local

# --- Illustrative image generation (server-side only) ---
# Default: OFF. The report works without any of these; the "Before and illustrative
# after" section then shows its calm placeholder. When on, an image is generated
# ONLY after the person clicks "Generate My Illustrative View" and agrees to send
# their front photo to OpenAI, and only for a change MogaFace has approved
# (see lib/visualization/eligibility.ts). The route (app/api/generate-illustration)
# also refuses every request in production until an authenticator and a
# shared-store rate limiter exist. The photo is held in memory for one request
# and is never stored or logged. Uses the same OPENAI_API_KEY as the wording provider.
# IMAGE_GENERATION_PROVIDER=       # unset (off) or "openai"
# OPENAI_API_KEY=                  # never commit a real key; put it in .env.local
# IMAGE_GENERATION_MODEL=          # optional image model id; default is the constant in lib/image-generation/openaiImages.ts
# IMAGE_GENERATION_SIZE=           # optional, e.g. 1024x1536 (default: chosen from the photo's orientation)
# IMAGE_GENERATION_QUALITY=        # optional, e.g. medium
# IMAGE_GENERATION_INPUT_FIDELITY= # optional identity-fidelity setting, e.g. high
# IMAGE_GENERATION_TIMEOUT_MS=     # optional; 10000-58000, default 55000
# IMAGE_GENERATION_API_KEY=        # only for other vendors registered in lib/image-generation/provider.ts; the OpenAI provider does not use it
# The browser only shows the generate button when this public, non-secret flag is "1":
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ILLUSTRATION_GENERATION=

# --- Consultation button on the results page (public, not secret) ---
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONSULTATION_URL=        # https://, mailto:, tel: or a site path; default "/"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONSULTATION_CTA_LABEL=  # default "Discuss My Results"

# --- AI wording for the personalised report (server-side only) ---
# Default: OFF. With none of these set, the deterministic local rules write the
# whole report and nothing is sent to any third party. OpenAI (Responses API)
# only rephrases a deterministic draft; every evidence reference, status,
# category and limitation stays exactly as the local engine produced it, and
# anything invalid, slow or failing is discarded in favour of the local text.
# Server-side only: NEVER prefix the key or model with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# The endpoint (app/api/interpret) also refuses every request in production
# until an authenticator and a shared-store rate limiter exist, and until the
# person has consented — see docs/INTERPRETATION_AND_RESULTS.md.
# INTERPRETATION_PROVIDER=        # unset or "local" (default), or "openai"
# OPENAI_API_KEY=                 # never commit a real key; put it in .env.local
# INTERPRETATION_MODEL=           # optional text model id; default is the constant in lib/interpretation/openai.ts
# INTERPRETATION_TIMEOUT_MS=      # optional; 1000-25000, default 20000

# The browser only calls the endpoint when this public, non-secret flag is "1"
# AND the person's consent is "granted" (no consent screen exists yet).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_INTERPRETATION_REMOTE=
